# {{ dist }}

An **unofficial**, typed {{ "Python" if lang == "python" else "TypeScript" }} client for
[{{ spec.domain }}]({{ spec.base_url }}), generated by
[Ghost API](https://github.com/Danielraj5605/Ghost-api) {{ version }} from the site's own
traffic. It is not made or supported by {{ spec.domain }}: the API can change without notice,
and the site's terms of service apply. Regenerate it with `ghost-api refresh {{ spec.domain }}`.

## Install

{% if lang == "python" %}
```bash
pip install path/to/package/python        # or vendor src/{{ module }}/ into your project
```

Needs Python 3.10+, `httpx` and `pydantic` (installed with it).
{% else %}
```bash
npm install path/to/package/typescript     # builds dist/ on install
```

Made for Node 18+ (servers, scripts, serverless functions). In a web page, browsers block
reading another site's replies unless it allows CORS, and don't let code set the
User-Agent: call this client from your own server instead.
{% endif %}

## Use it

{% if lang == "python" %}
```python
from {{ module }} import {{ spec.class_name }}

with {{ spec.class_name }}() as api:
{% if methods %}
    result = api.{{ methods[0].method.name }}({{ methods[0].py_args }})
{% endif %}
```

The same methods with asyncio:

```python
from {{ module }} import {{ spec.async_class }}

async with {{ spec.async_class }}() as api:
{% if methods %}
    result = await api.{{ methods[0].method.name }}({{ methods[0].py_args }})
{% endif %}
```
{% else %}
```ts
import { {{ spec.class_name }} } from "{{ dist }}";

const api = new {{ spec.class_name }}();
{% if methods %}
const result = await api.{{ methods[0].ts_name }}({{ methods[0].ts_args }});
{% endif %}
```
{% endif %}
