## Errors

Every failure is a `{{ spec.error_class }}` with `.status` (0 for network errors) and
`.body`. Catch one kind with its subclass:

| Error | When |
|---|---|
| `{{ spec.error_classes.auth }}` | 401 / 403, or a missing credential |
| `{{ spec.error_classes.not_found }}` | 404 |
| `{{ spec.error_classes.rate_limit }}` | 429 after the retries |
| `{{ spec.error_classes.server }}` | 5xx after the retries |

## Manners

The client sends at most one request per second by default
(`{{ "max_requests_per_second" if lang == "python" else "maxRequestsPerSecond" }}`), retries
429 and 5xx with backoff (`{{ "max_retries" if lang == "python" else "maxRetries" }}`), and
identifies itself with a User-Agent naming Ghost API. Keep it that way: it's someone else's
server.
